---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { APP } from '../../config';
import { ROUTES } from '../../i18n';
---

<PageLayout
  locale="en"
  title="Support"
  description="Help with Ride Streak: common issues with Apple Health, Strava and the Garage — and how to reach us."
  paths={ROUTES.support}
  intro="Just write to us. The developer answers, not a ticket system."
>
  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      <strong>Email:</strong>
      <a href={`mailto:${APP.supportEmail}?subject=Ride%20Streak%20Support`}
        >{APP.supportEmail}</a
      >
    </p>
    <p>
      Useful to include: your iOS version, the app version (Settings → at the
      bottom) and, if it concerns a specific ride, its date.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Common cases</h2>

  <h3>No rides are showing up</h3>
  <p>
    Ride Streak reads from Apple Health only. Check Settings → Privacy &amp;
    Security → Health → Ride Streak and make sure every category is enabled.
    Without permission for "Workouts" the list stays empty. Rides that only
    exist in a manufacturer's app and are never written to Apple Health cannot
    reach the app — that is what the optional Strava connection is for.
  </p>

  <h3>Power, cadence or segments are missing</h3>
  <p>
    Apple Health does not carry these values. Connect Strava in Settings so
    Ride Streak can pull them from your bike computer.
  </p>

  <h3>The Garage is not counting kilometres</h3>
  <p>
    Parts only count from their install date, and only for rides assigned to
    that bike. Check your assignment rules, or assign rides retroactively with
    "Assign rides by date".
  </p>

  <h3>Restore purchases</h3>
  <p>
    Open Settings in the app and tap "Restore purchases". You need the same
    Apple ID the purchase was made with. Refunds run exclusively through
    <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com" rel="noopener" target="_blank"
      >reportaproblem.apple.com</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h3>Cancel a subscription</h3>
  <p>
    iPhone Settings → your name → Subscriptions → Ride Streak. Every free
    feature stays available afterwards.
  </p>

  <h3>Delete your account and cloud data</h3>
  <p>
    If you enabled RideStreak Cloud you can delete your account and all
    server-side data directly in the app's settings. Without Cloud there is no
    account — deleting the app is enough.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
